 "markdown": "## Summary\nChange the dashboard's page title text from \"Customer Dashboard\" to \"Customer Dashboard 26C\".\n\n## How it works today\nThe page uses the `oj-sp-general-overview-page` template, and the heading shown at the top of the page comes from its `page-title` attribute, which is currently set to `\"Customer Dashboard\"`.\n\n## What changes\nOnly the displayed page title text needs to change to the requested value.\n\n## The change\n- `webApps/vbredwoodapp/flows/customer-portal/pages/customer-dashboard-page.html` — update the `page-title` attribute value to `Customer Dashboard 26C`.\n\n## After the change\nWhen a customer opens the dashboard, the header at the top of the page will read \"Customer Dashboard 26C\" instead of \"Customer Dashboard\". Everything else (tiles, table, navigation) behaves exactly as before.\n\n## Risks\nNone known — only the display text of this one page's header changes; no chains, variables, or endpoints are affected.\n\n## How to test\n1. Open the app and navigate to `/vp/shell/customer-portal/customer-dashboard`.\n2. Confirm the large heading at the top of the page reads \"Customer Dashboard 26C\".\n3. Confirm the subtitle, KPI tiles, and Recent Activity table all still appear and work.\n\n## Questions\nNone",
